*value = "Acclaim Entertainment, Inc. Presents\nVEXX  \nAll Rights Reserved\nDeveloped by Acclaim Studios Austin.\n   &   2003 Acclaim Entertainment, Inc.\nLicensed by Nintendo.\n\n"
*key = 53
*value = "Beyond the curtain falls\nModel castle comes to light\nTo scale the tower's walls\nMind what is out of sight"
*key = 54
*value = "Cursed heart just out of reach\nBehind a crystal veil\nIf molten trick we didn't teach\nThis run will not avail"
*key = 55
*value = "When hearts did burst asunder\nMuch Energy did scatter\nTo return this heart its thunder\nOne hundred's all that matters"
*key = 56
*value = "What once was ancient swells\nA sea did drain below\nTo find it down the wells\nYou'll find you have to go"
*key = 57
*value = "Where Dragon's heart did beat\nA doorway with suspense\nWithin use Talons' heat\nTo loose some things immense"
*key = 58
*value = "Again a heart in sight\nIs locked within clear walls\nWithout your molten might\nIt remains beyond your calls"
*key = 59
*value = "Within Timberdale spire\nWhile moving hand o'er hand\nAccess you'll acquire\nTo this castle of sand"
*key = 60
*value = "A drop into a well\nIs followed by a splash\nBeware the fish are fell\nElectric is their lash"
*key = 61
*value = "Shadowed alcove through\nA game of gatherings\nCollect more than a few\nTo win at Temple Rings"
*key = 62
*value = "Above Dark Cavern floats\nHeart teasingly so near\nTo get high above the moats\nHope flying's not your fear"
*key = 63
*value = "Over shadowed pools in gloom\nLifeless eyes are dark\nIn sockets fire will bloom\nIf lightning there does arc"
*key = 64
*value = "It's in plain sight to find\nBut not without some luck\nIn the interest of being kind\nThrough top of box you duck"
*key = 65
*value = "This tower's tiny clone\nIs sleeping with the fishes\nCatch the rings as they're thrown\nDefeat yourself for wishes"
*key = 66
*value = "Deep in a boiling well\nAbove the ghastly steamer\nClimb to the peak of hell\nA heart there seeks redeemer"
*key = 67
*value = "In the belly of the beast\nShort's chest deserves a look\nThe key to its release\nIs hidden in the book"
*key = 68
*value = "A chamber full of blocks\nIs built to drive you mad\nTo climb them choose your knocks\nOr you'll find that you've been had"
*key = 69
*value = "A sandy theme for certain\nNeeds a Mummy to take a fall\nBeyond the stony curtain\nYou're sure to have a ball"
*key = 70
*value = "In the lowly lake\nLie some rings so cheesy\nA task you'll think is cake\nYou'll find is not so easy"
*key = 71
*value = "In Summit of the Sages\nThrough pumphouse hidden door\nFor heart that's hid for ages\nJust Hop and Drop some more"
*key = 72
*value = "A chamber unexpected\nLies deep beneath the ice\nIf you are not deflected\nA heart will be your vice"
*key = 73
*value = "Spilling 'cross the sky\nPerilous platforms float\nNear icy gusts they fly\nIn fact, above them note"
*key = 74
*value = "I'm Nasty."
*key = 75
*value = "My name is Brutish."
*key = 76
*value = "They call me Short."
*key = 77
*value = "Move around using the <7> left analog stick. You can change the<pause>speed at which you move by applying more or less pressure to the <7> left analog stick. <pause>Try moving to the end of the walkway in front of you."
*key = 78
*value = "Well done. Now, try navigating this area ahead of you to get to the end."
*key = 79
*value = "Journal Entry 1:  This morning, father gave me this journal. It's a gift to mark this special day, the day he was appointed Guardian of Astara.  Father has trained for years so his wisdom and strength will nurture peace as we seek greater discoveries and understanding.  Mother is so proud of him.  Now, our greatest scientists are preparing a marvelous travel system. I'm told it will open a giant hole in space, so we can visit other worlds."
*key = 80
*value = "Journal Entry 2:  I'm so scared; I can hardly hold the pen steady.  We had a big celebration and then opened the rift, but on the other side evil creatures were waiting to attack.  A war has started. Father went to fight these demons that call themselves Shadowraiths. IЕ I saw one wraith named Yabu kill my mother and my sisters.  I can't get it out of my mind.  I wanted to fight this Yabu, but the wraiths have absorbed all of the energy from the rift system and grown very strong. Father locked me inside the Landspire, and said to not let anyone, or anything, inside."
*key = 81
*value = "Journal Entry 3:  I can't sleep; all I hear are screams and cries outside. The wraiths are sucking the life force out of our world. They drain the souls from their victims, and keep them in these horrible jars.  I want to leave the Landspire and fight with Father, but he said I'm too young, and it's more important that I keep the keystaff safely away from the wraiths.  Through the eyehole, I saw father fighting another Astana, but it turned out to be a wraith. He came back later, and told me to bring the keystaff out, but it wasn't really himЕ It was another wraith trying to trick me.  It's so hard to know who to trust when these things can change their shape like this."
*key = 82
*value = "Journal Entry 4:  The screams have stopped; it's so quiet now. I disobeyed father, and went outside.  Our world is torn to bits, and pieces of it are scattered across the sky.  My nightmares were trueЕ Father is dead. I found him clutching a spire of rock, the talons imbedded in it; I guess he wanted to keep the War Talons from the wraiths at the end. At least all of the wraiths seem to be gone; grotesque beating hearts are all that remain of them."
*key = 83
*value = "Journal Entry 5:  Dark Yabu is alive! He's built a fortress in the far reaches of Astara's ruins.  In some twisted way, his citadel actually lives and has sucked the energy out of the world around it like a parasite.  The land nearby has become even more desolate and cold than it already was.  Strangely, the thought of Yabu living consoles meЕ perhaps if he survived, some of my own people may live yet somewhereЕ  I now have a quest.  I will show Yabu the same mercy he showed my family."
*key = 84
*value = "Journal Entry 6:  I have visited what remains of Astara. My people are gone.  I'm the last one. The life that once lived here has become dark and twisted.  Those vile Wraithhearts still beat with life. The wraiths sucked the energy out of the Rift Gate System and it seems to live on in these wicked vessels.  The portal gates still stand and the system can be recharged; the main portal could be opened again. I can never let this happen."
*key = 85
*value = "Journal Entry 7:  A new civilization grows amongst the treetops in a corner of Astara they call the Overwood.  As I studied their simple culture, I found myself moved by the respect with which they regard their world and each other.  I thought of my people and how foolish and prideful we were. These people are content with their peaceful lives. I hope that peace remains."
*key = 86
*value = "Journal Entry 8:  Something terrible is coming. After all this time, Dark Yabu is moving about Astara, searching.  He seems to have collected an army of beasts from the Shadowrealm. I fear he is trying to collect the Wraithhearts to re-open the gate and bring back his fellow Wraiths.  But, I discovered that, for some reason, Yabu cannot touch the hearts, or even get close to them.  I've hidden as many of them as I can, although I can't find some of them myself.  Perhaps Yabu is searching for someone to complete this gruesome collection for him."
*key = 87
*value = "Journal Entry 9:  My worst fears are realized. Yabu has discovered the people of Overwood and is heading towards them. Does he mean to make them perform his cursed errand and collect the hearts?  I fear there is nothing I can do to help the peaceful people. Their guardian, Vargas, is old and no match for Yabu and his creatures.  I hope there is one among them that can stand up to Yabu's wickedness, but I fear the worst."
*key = 88
*value = "Excellent. In order to JUMP, press the <3> button."
*key = 89
*value = "Excellent. You can use the JUMP to move across gaps by pushing the <pause><7> left analog stick towards the area you wish to JUMP<pause> to, and pressing the <3> button. Try jumping across this gap."
*key = 90
*value = "Two WRAITHHEARTS are required to activate this button."
*key = 100
*value = "You will often come across gaps that are too wide for you to JUMP across normally. <pause>You can use the LONG JUMP to cross these chasms. <pause>To execute the LONG JUMP, first push the <7> left analog stick to run towards your destination. <pause>Then, hold down the <9> button followed by pressing the <3> button."
*key = 101
*value = "Nicely done.  Try using the LONG JUMP to get across this area."
*key = 102
*value = "If you want to JUMP higher than usual, you can perform the PULSE JUMP. <pause>First, hold down the <9> button to CROUCH.  Next, press the <3> button while still crouching. <pause>Try using the PULSE JUMP to get on top of this structure."
*key = 103
*value = "Try using the PULSE JUMP to get on top of this structure."
*key = 104
*value = "Vexx..."
*key = 105
*value = "...Open your eyes..."
*key = 106
*value = "You have endured so much, and yet your journey has only just begun."
*key = 107
*value = "...Vexx..."
*key = 108
*value = "Once you are underwater, you can SWIM by holding down the <4><pause>button while steering with the <7> left analog stick. Hold the <4> button lightly to SWIM slowly,<pause>and hold the <4> button down with more pressure to SWIM quickly.<pause>On the surface of the water, steer using the <7> left analog stick,<pause>and tap the <4> button repeatedly to move forward. Try swimming to the door at the bottom of this pool."
*key = 109
*value = "The War Talons allow you to CLIMB sheer walls that look similar to the one in front of you.<pause>JUMP onto the wall, then press the <7> left analog stick towards the direction <pause>in which you wish to move. You can jump up, down, left, or right <pause>by holding the <7> left analog stick in a direction and pressing the <3> button.<pause>To jump outwards off of the wall, leave the <7> left analog stick <pause>in the neutral position and press the <3> button."
